<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka nets $7 mln from estate privatisation.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka nets $7 mln from estate privatisation.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka sold its controlling stake in Namunukula Plantations for $7.03 million on the Colombo Stock Exchange on Thursday, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The government sold its 51 percent holding in the company at 40 rupees a 10-rupee share to Keells Plantation Management Services, said one broker.</p>
</text>
